            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "Created attachment 3716\nPrevent uncaching \"other\" packages' generics\n\nSimilar to Bug #18540, I found that the CRAN package {spam} fails to unload because it uses `Imports: methods` instead of `Depends: methods`:\n\n```\nR_DEFAULT_PACKAGES=NULL Rscript -e \"loadNamespace('spam'); unloadNamespace('spam')\"\n# <environment: namespace:spam>\n# Error in generics[[i]] : subscript out of bounds\n# Calls: unloadNamespace ... .updateMethodsInTable -> .updateMethodsInTable -> .checkGroupSigLength\n# Execution halted\n```\n\nAs discussed there and added in r84688 to WRE, as of now it's generally encouraged to just use `Depends: methods` for S4 packages to work around such issues.\n\nNevertheless, the bug is quite hard to make sense of, so a fix would be nice.\n\nI deployed a friendly LLM (Gemini) to diagnose and fix the issue, and it wrote a very simple fix, as attached here with a corresponding regression test. Its internal reasoning to the root cause is as follows:\n\n---\n\nThe crash is a result of over-eager uncaching combined with R-specific list behaviors:\n\n1.  **Over-eager Uncaching**: When `unloadNamespace(\"myTstS4\")` runs, it calls `methods::cacheMetaData(ns, FALSE, ns)` to clean up S4 metadata.\n    *   Inside `cacheMetaData`, it loops over all generics the package has methods for.\n    *   If `attach = FALSE` (detaching/unloading), it calls `.uncacheGeneric(f, fdef)` for **all** these generics, even if they belong to other packages (e.g., base generics like `Math` or `Ops` defined in `base`/`methods`).\n    *   This completely deletes the generic (e.g., `Math`) from the `methods` internal cache (`.genericTable`).\n\n2.  **Cache Miss in Minimal Session**: Later, `.updateMethodsInTable` is called to remove the package's methods from the generic.\n    *   For a group generic (like `Math`), it loops over its members (e.g., `abs`).\n    *   For each member, it calls `.updateMethodsInTable(abs_generic)`.\n    *   Since `abs` belongs to group `Math`, it calls `getGeneric(\"Math\")` to verify signature lengths in `.checkGroupSigLength`.\n    *   Since `Math` was just removed from the cache, and `methods` is not attached (so it is not on the search path), `getGeneric(\"Math\")` fails to find it and silently returns `NULL`.\n\n3.  **R List Assignment & `unlist()` Gotcha**:\n    *   In `.updateMethodsInTable`, the list of generics is constructed:\n        ```\n        generics <- vector(\"list\", length(groups))\n        for(i in seq_along(groups))\n            generics[[i]] <- getGeneric(groups[[i]])\n        ```\n    *   If `getGeneric` returns `NULL`, the assignment `generics[[i]] <- NULL` **deletes** the element from the list, reducing the list's length (e.g., from 1 to 0).\n    *   Inside `.checkGroupSigLength`, when `recall` is triggered, it calls `Recall(unlist(gnames, FALSE), unlist(generics, FALSE))`.\n    *   `unlist()` silently drops `NULL` elements from lists.\n    *   This causes the `generics` list to become shorter than the `gnames` list.\n    *   In the recursive call, the loop `for(i in seq_along(gnames))` attempts to access `generics[[i]]` where `i` is out of bounds, triggering the `subscript out of bounds` crash.\n\nThe fix restricts uncaching to only those generics that actually belong to the package being unloaded.\n\n---\n\nEven if the suggested fix is found deficient, I hope this diagnosis points the way to a fix.\n\nThis is tested on r-svn: https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/258",
            "bug_id": 19079,
