            "bug_id": 19079,
            "text": "Thanks for the report and the suggested fix.\n\nOne thing to watch out for with S4 generics is that `@package` points to the package defining the function that the generic represents. So for example if a package does `setGeneric(\"nrow\", ...)`, `@package` will be \"base\", and with this fix, the `nrow()` methods would remain. \n\nWhy not see what your friend does with that feedback :)",
            "creation_time": "2026-05-29T00:38:59Z",
            "creator": "lawremi"
          },
          {
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": 3717,
            "time": "2026-05-29T06:28:25Z",
            "creation_time": "2026-05-29T06:28:25Z",
            "bug_id": 19079,
            "text": "Created attachment 3717\nUpdated patch for unloading generics without methods to handle e.g. base generics better\n\nGreat point! I was content to just let the unload process only finish partially in that case, but indeed our friend was able to push further by looking for the definition in the correct environment.\n\nUpdated here and on GitHub with a new test case ensuring `nrow()` reverts to non-generic after unloading the test package: `stopifnot(!isGeneric('nrow'))`",
